---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import '../styles/global.css';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import RockTable from '../components/RockTable.astro';
---

<Base title="What is Stratum? Multi-Tenancy Library for Node.js" description="Stratum is an open-source multi-tenancy library for Node.js and TypeScript. Hierarchical tenants, config inheritance, three isolation strategies, GDPR compliance. Learn why we built it and how it works.">

<Nav />

<!-- Editorial entry: quiet, starts with a scenario -->
<section class="wis-hero">
  <p class="wis-lede">
    You shipped multi-tenancy with a <code>tenant_id</code> column six months ago.
    Now your biggest customer wants isolated data, your compliance team needs audit logs,
    and the new reseller deal requires nested organizations three levels deep.
  </p>
  <h1>That is the problem <span class="accent">Stratum</span> solves.</h1>
  <p class="wis-elevator">
    An open-source multi-tenancy library for Node.js and TypeScript.
    Hierarchical tenants, config inheritance, permission delegation,
    three database isolation strategies, and GDPR compliance, from day one.
  </p>
</section>

<!-- The Problem -->
<section class="wis-section">
  <h2>The problem Stratum solves</h2>
  <p class="wis-intro">
    Every B2B SaaS team starts the same way: add a <code>tenant_id</code> column to every table.
    It works, until your product grows.
  </p>

  <div class="wis-timeline">
    <div class="wis-timeline-item">
      <div class="wis-timeline-marker"></div>
      <div class="wis-timeline-content">
        <h3>Day 1</h3>
        <p><code>tenant_id</code> on every table, manual WHERE clauses. Simple. Works fine.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="wis-timeline-item">
      <div class="wis-timeline-marker wis-warning"></div>
      <div class="wis-timeline-content">
        <h3>Month 6</h3>
        <p>Enterprise customer needs custom configuration. You hand-roll config tables with no inheritance. Each customer is a special case.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="wis-timeline-item">
      <div class="wis-timeline-marker wis-warning"></div>
      <div class="wis-timeline-content">
        <h3>Month 12</h3>
        <p>Compliance audit. You scramble to add audit logging, data export, and purge capabilities. Retroactively.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="wis-timeline-item">
      <div class="wis-timeline-marker wis-danger"></div>
      <div class="wis-timeline-content">
        <h3>Later</h3>
        <p>Large customer demands data isolation. Painful migration from shared tables to schema-per-tenant. Engineering time for each piece.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="wis-punchline">
    The cost comes later. As the product grows, your team builds a weaker version of Stratum and spends engineering time on each piece.
    Stratum gives you all of this from day one.
  </p>
</section>

<!-- How It Works -->
<section class="wis-section wis-how">
  <h2>How Stratum works</h2>

  <div class="wis-feature-grid">
    <!-- Tenant Hierarchy -->
    <div class="wis-feature-card layer">
      <h3>Tenant hierarchy</h3>
      <p>
        Tenants form a tree. A root organization can have resellers, who have clients,
        who have teams. Config and permissions flow down the tree automatically.
      </p>
      <!-- The same tenant tree as the homepage hero: one rock band per tenant,
           colored by depth and indented under its parent. -->
      <ol class="inherit-tree wis-tree" aria-label="Example tenant hierarchy">
        <li class="itrow d0"><span class="idepth">d0</span><span class="inode">AcmeSec</span><span class="imeta">root</span></li>
        <li class="itrow d1"><span class="idepth">d1</span><span class="inode">NorthStar MSP</span><span class="imeta">reseller</span></li>
        <li class="itrow d2"><span class="idepth">d2</span><span class="inode">client-alpha</span></li>
        <li class="itrow d2"><span class="idepth">d2</span><span class="inode">client-beta</span></li>
        <li class="itrow d1"><span class="idepth">d1</span><span class="inode">Apex Partners</span></li>
        <li class="itrow d2"><span class="idepth">d2</span><span class="inode">client-gamma</span></li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <!-- Config Inheritance -->
    <div class="wis-feature-card layer">
      <h3>Config inheritance</h3>
      <p>
        Set a value on the root tenant and every child inherits it automatically.
        Lock a key so children can't override it. Override it at any level when needed.
      </p>
      <!-- The homepage config rows (.icfg): the inherited value is vein, the
           locked key is magma. The child rows indent under the root. -->
      <div class="inherit-config wis-config">
        <div class="icfg"><span class="ikey">root: max_users = 1000</span><span class="itag">&larr; set once</span></div>
        <div class="icfg icfg-resolved wis-cfg-child"><span class="ikey">&boxvr;&boxh; child-a: <span class="ival">inherits 1000</span></span><span class="itag">&larr; automatic</span></div>
        <div class="icfg wis-cfg-child"><span class="ikey">&boxur;&boxh; child-b: max_users = 500</span><span class="itag">&larr; override</span></div>
        <div class="icfg icfg-locked"><span class="ikey">root: <span class="accent">region = "eu" (locked)</span></span><span class="itag">&larr; children cannot change</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Isolation Strategies -->
    <div class="wis-feature-card wis-feature-wide layer">
      <h3>Three isolation strategies</h3>
      <p>
        Choose per tenant. Mix strategies in a single deployment.
        Upgrade a tenant's isolation level without migrating data.
      </p>
      <!-- The homepage depth gauge: the three strategies as one stack of rock,
           shallow to deep. -->
      <div class="isolation-stack wis-isolation">
        <div class="isolation-row iso-rls">
          <div class="isolation-face">
            <span><span class="isolation-label">Shared RLS</span><span class="wis-isolation-desc">Same tables, PostgreSQL Row-Level Security. Lowest cost, highest density.</span></span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="isolation-row iso-schema">
          <div class="isolation-face">
            <span><span class="isolation-label">Schema</span><span class="wis-isolation-desc">Separate schema per tenant. Stronger isolation, still one database.</span></span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="isolation-row iso-db">
          <div class="isolation-face">
            <span><span class="isolation-label">Database</span><span class="wis-isolation-desc">Dedicated PostgreSQL instance. Maximum isolation for compliance.</span></span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Why We Built It -->
<section class="wis-section">
  <h2>Why we built Stratum</h2>
  <p>
    We've seen multi-tenancy pain firsthand, at security platforms (MSSP/MSP) where
    nested tenant hierarchies are the norm, and at B2B SaaS companies where enterprise
    customers demand isolation, custom config, and compliance.
  </p>
  <p>
    Every team we worked with had the same story: they started with <code>tenant_id</code>,
    then built config tables, then added audit logs, then scrambled for isolation,
    each time reinventing what should be infrastructure.
  </p>
  <p>
    The Node.js and TypeScript ecosystem has no dominant multi-tenancy library.
    The .NET world has <a href="https://abp.io" class="wis-link">ABP.IO</a>.
    Ruby has <a href="https://github.com/influitive/apartment" class="wis-link">Apartment</a>.
    Node.js developers roll their own every time. Stratum changes that.
  </p>
</section>

<!-- Comparison -->
<section class="wis-section">
  <h2>Stratum vs alternatives</h2>
  <RockTable
    label="Comparison of multi-tenancy approaches"
    columns={["Capability", "Stratum", "tenant_id column", "WorkOS / Frontegg", "Custom built"]}
    rows={[
      { feat: "Tenant hierarchy", cells: [["good", "Yes"], ["bad", "No"], ["bad", "No"], ["neutral", "Build it yourself"]] },
      { feat: "Config inheritance", cells: [["good", "Built-in"], ["bad", "No"], ["bad", "No"], ["neutral", "Build it yourself"]] },
      { feat: "Isolation strategies", cells: [["good", "3 (RLS, schema, DB)"], ["neutral", "Manual RLS"], ["bad", "No"], ["neutral", "Build it yourself"]] },
      { feat: "GDPR compliance", cells: [["good", "Export + purge"], ["bad", "No"], ["neutral", "Partial"], ["neutral", "Build it yourself"]] },
      { feat: "Audit logging", cells: [["good", "Built-in"], ["bad", "No"], ["neutral", "Auth events only"], ["neutral", "Build it yourself"]] },
      { feat: "Setup", cells: [["good", "npm install and initialize()"], ["neutral", "A column and a filter on every query"], ["neutral", "1 week"], ["bad", "Engineering time for each piece"]] },
      { feat: "Open source", cells: [["good", "MIT"], ["good", "N/A"], ["bad", "Proprietary"], ["good", "Yours"]] },
    ]}
  />
</section>

<!-- Getting Started -->
<section class="wis-section wis-getting-started">
  <h2>Get started in 5 lines</h2>
  <div class="code-block">
    <div class="code-block-header">
      <span class="code-block-filename">quickstart.ts</span>
    </div>
    <pre set:html={`<span class="kw">import</span> &#123; Pool &#125; <span class="kw">from</span> <span class="str">"pg"</span>;
<span class="kw">import</span> &#123; Stratum &#125; <span class="kw">from</span> <span class="str">"@stratum-hq/lib"</span>;

<span class="kw">const</span> stratum = <span class="kw">new</span> <span class="fn">Stratum</span>(&#123; pool: <span class="kw">new</span> <span class="fn">Pool</span>(), autoMigrate: <span class="num">true</span> &#125;);
<span class="kw">await</span> stratum.<span class="fn">initialize</span>();

<span class="cm">// Create a tenant and set config</span>
<span class="kw">const</span> org = <span class="kw">await</span> stratum.<span class="fn">createOrganization</span>(&#123; name: <span class="str">"Acme Corp"</span>, slug: <span class="str">"acme"</span> &#125;);
<span class="kw">await</span> stratum.<span class="fn">setConfig</span>(org.id, <span class="str">"max_users"</span>, &#123; value: <span class="num">100</span> &#125;);
<span class="cm">// That's it. Multi-tenancy with config inheritance, ready to go.</span>`} />
  </div>
</section>

<!-- CTA -->
<section class="cta">
  <div class="cta-inner fade-in">
    <h2>Ready to stop reinventing <span class="accent">multi-tenancy?</span></h2>
    <div class="hero-actions" style="justify-content: center;">
      <a href="https://docs.stratum-hq.org/getting-started/quick-start/" class="btn-primary">Get Started</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/stratum-hq/Stratum" class="btn-secondary">GitHub</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<Footer />

<style>
  /* What-is-Stratum page styles */
  .wis-hero {
    max-width: 700px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: calc(var(--space-8) * 4) var(--space-6) var(--space-12);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .wis-lede {
    font-size: 1.1875rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
    max-width: 60ch;
    margin-left: auto;
    margin-right: auto;
  }

  .wis-lede code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.875em;
    color: var(--code-text);
    background: var(--code-bg);
    padding: 2px 6px;
  }

  .wis-hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 5vw, 2.75rem);
    font-weight: 900;
    line-height: 0.95;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
    color: var(--text-primary);
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .wis-elevator {
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    max-width: 58ch;
    margin-left: auto;
    margin-right: auto;
  }

  /* A full width keeps the section inside the viewport: see "body > main" in
     global.css for why an auto-margined child of body needs one. */
  .wis-section {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 700px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--space-8) var(--space-6);
  }

  .wis-section h2 {
    font-size: 2.125rem;
    font-weight: 900;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
    color: var(--text-primary);
    text-align: center;
    line-height: 0.95;
  }

  .wis-section p {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .wis-section code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.875em;
    color: var(--code-text);
    background: var(--code-bg);
    padding: 2px 6px;
  }

  .wis-intro {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
  }

  .wis-punchline {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-weight: 500;
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
    text-align: center;
  }

  /* Timeline */
  .wis-timeline {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 2.5rem;
    margin: var(--space-6) auto;
    max-width: 500px;
  }

  .wis-timeline::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 7px;
    top: 4px;
    bottom: 4px;
    width: 2px;
    background: var(--border);
  }

  .wis-timeline-item {
    position: relative;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }

  .wis-timeline-marker {
    position: absolute;
    left: -2rem;
    top: 6px;
    width: 16px;
    height: 16px;
    background: var(--surface-2);
    border: 2px solid var(--sandstone);
  }

  .wis-timeline-marker.wis-warning {
    border-color: var(--warning);
  }

  .wis-timeline-marker.wis-danger {
    border-color: var(--error);
    background: var(--accent-muted);
  }

  .wis-timeline-content h3 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .wis-timeline-content p {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* How Stratum works: breakout section, wider than text sections */
  .wis-how {
    max-width: 1100px;
    margin-left: auto;
    margin-right: auto;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    padding-left: var(--space-6);
    padding-right: var(--space-6);
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  .wis-how h2 {
    text-align: center;
    width: 100%;
    line-height: 0.95;
  }

  @media (max-width: 1100px) {
    .wis-how {
      max-width: 100%;
    }
  }

  /* Feature grid */
  /* minmax(0, 1fr): a plain 1fr column grows to fit the widest diagram line,
     which pushed the page past the viewport. The diagrams scroll instead. */
  .wis-feature-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-4);
    width: 100%;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .wis-feature-grid {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }

  /* Each card is a ledge panel (.layer in global.css). The top padding
     clears the 10px rock lip. */
  .wis-feature-card {
    padding: calc(var(--space-6) + 10px) var(--space-6) var(--space-6);
  }

  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .wis-feature-card {
      padding-left: var(--space-4);
      padding-right: var(--space-4);
    }
  }

  .wis-feature-card h3 {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .wis-feature-card p {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .wis-feature-wide {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
  }

  .wis-config {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
  }

  .wis-cfg-child {
    margin-left: 28px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .wis-cfg-child {
      margin-left: 14px;
    }
  }

  .wis-tree,
  .wis-isolation {
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
  }

  .wis-isolation-desc {
    display: block;
    margin-top: var(--space-1);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .wis-link {
    color: var(--sandstone);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .wis-link:hover {
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  /* Getting Started */
  .wis-getting-started {
    max-width: 700px;
  }

  .wis-getting-started h2 {
    text-align: center;
    line-height: 0.95;
  }
</style>


</Base>
